      "page_num": 1,
      "width": 595.2755737304688,
      "height": 841.8897705078125,
      "text": "<b>QP No.</b><br/>QP-\nMECH-001\n<b>Issue\nDate</b><br/>15-09-2026\n<b>Revision\nNo.</b><br/>A\n<b>Date</b><br/>15-09\n-2026\n<b>Name</b><br/>A. Kulkarni\nCOSO\nMECHANICAL DRIVE SHAFT ENGINEERING SPECIFICATION\n<b>Document Code:</b> MECH-001 &nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Discipline:</b> Mechanical &nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Classification:</b> Training / Test\n1. Scope\nThis engineering specification defines requirements for precision machining, dimensional inspection and documentation of a centrifugal\npump drive shaft.\n2. Material Requirements\nShaft material shall be alloy steel suitable for continuous industrial service. Material certificates shall be traceable to the heat number.\n3. Dimensional Requirements\nParameter\nNominal\nTolerance\nUnit\nInspection Method\nOverall Length\n850.00\n\u00b10.50\nmm\nVernier / CMM\nJournal Diameter\n75.00\n\u00b10.03\nmm\nMicrometer\nKeyway Width\n18.00\n\u00b10.05\nmm\nGauge\nRunout\n0.00\n\u22640.05\nmm\nDial Indicator\n4. Surface Finish\nJournal surface finish shall be Ra 1.6 \u00b5m maximum. The shaft shall be free from visible burrs, cracks and machining damage.\n5. Operating Conditions\nMaximum operating temperature: 80.0 \u00b0C. Maximum operating pressure: 10 bar. Continuous rated speed: 1480 rpm.\n6. Inspection and Records\nInspection results shall identify the measured value, unit, instrument identification, calibration status and inspector. Any out-of-tolerance\nresult shall be recorded as a nonconformance.\n7. Table of Contents Reference\n1 Scope ........ 1\n2 Material Requirements ........ 1\n3 Dimensional Requirements ........ 2\n4 Surface Finish ........ 2\n5 Operating Conditions ........ 2\n6 Inspection and Records ........ 3\nSpecGuard Training/Test Document | MECH-001\nPage 1",
